#
# Vendor pins are byte-exact: `vendor/floorplan/CHECKSUMS.sha256` is checked
# against the working-tree bytes by `tests/test_floorplan.py`, and git's own
# end-of-line conversion would make that hash depend on the reader's
# `core.autocrlf` rather than on the payload. A CI checkout with autocrlf on
# turned 49 of the 55 text files into CRLF and failed the pin, while a local
# checkout with it off passed: the same commit, two different byte streams.
#
# `-text` tells git to store and check these files out exactly as they are, so
# the checksums describe the payload and not the clone.
vendor/floorplan/** -text
